# API Configuration
# Copy this file to .env.local and update with your values.
#
# The browser calls SAME-ORIGIN paths only (`/v1/auth/...`, `/transactions-api/...`).
# `web/next.config.ts` rewrites those paths on to the two backends below, so the
# session cookie stays first-party and no CORS configuration is required on either
# backend (project.md NFR-base-6).
#
# Both variables are read server-side in next.config.ts only. They are deliberately
# NOT prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_ — a backend origin in the browser bundle is the
# anti-pattern called out in .claude/policies/bff-auth-pattern.md.
AUTH_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:10010
TRANSACTIONS_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:10005/transactions-api

# Optional. Overrides the base the shared API client prefixes to every request.
# Leave unset (or empty) so requests stay same-origin and go through the rewrites.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=

# Backend API Authentication
# Not used by this project: the Authentication API issues an HttpOnly `session`
# cookie that the browser attaches automatically (project.md §Authentication), so
# the frontend sets no auth header and holds no token.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_AUTH_HEADER controls the header name (e.g. Authorization, X-API-Key).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_AUTH_VALUE_PREFIX is the literal prefix prepended to the token
#   (include the trailing space if present, e.g. "Bearer ", or leave empty for raw keys).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_TOKEN holds the credential value.
#
# Note: NEXT_PUBLIC_* env vars are baked into the browser bundle. For production
# apps that talk to a real backend with sensitive tokens, prefer a BFF pattern
# (token stays server-side) or a Next.js API route proxy. The values below are
# intended for local development against a dev backend — see authentication-intake.md.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_AUTH_HEADER=Authorization
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_AUTH_VALUE_PREFIX=Bearer
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_TOKEN=
